# The agent-skill roots THIS tree keeps — read by scripts/skill-union-assert.sh when neither
# --roots nor $AGENT_SKILL_ROOTS is given (.github#517).
#
# FS-GG/.github is a KIT SOURCE repo, not a scaffolded product. ADR-0065 removes the former kit-lane
# exception: framework repos and scaffolded products expose the SAME runtime roots. The checked-in
# declaration keeps the bare local assertion and every materializer on that universal contract.
#
# TWO roots, not three (ADR-0065 as amended by ADR-0067 §5, landed by .github#1636). `.agents/skills`
# is CODEX's own second native root, not a third runtime's — measured on Codex CLI 0.145.0, which
# discovers it with no configuration at all. `.codex/skills` therefore carried no runtime the other
# two did not, and its only observable effect was a DUPLICATE catalog entry Codex emits when the same
# skill appears in both of its roots. Retiring it is a contract migration, not a mirror deletion.
.claude/skills
.agents/skills
